H29 gloss pass B (Opus vision, 28 Sept 2026, prompt scripts/PROMPTS.md "H29 gloss passes", independent of pass A). Rows verbatim. Its warning, verbatim: "four pairs of segment files are byte-identical (md5), so the cropper probably clamped at the same y: L03_s4 = L04_s4, L04_s2 = L05_s2, L05_s4 = L06_s4, L06_s1 = L07_s1 ... in most bands the gloss row is cut through at the top edge. Only the lower halves of the words show ... In L01_s1, L04_s2 (= L05_s2) and L05_s4 (= L06_s4), the clear words sit at cipher-row height and there are no cipher signs in that span. I marked them inline, but they may be the gloss row shifted by the crop offset." Per-band counts: L01 5, L02 6, L03 9, L04 8, L05 7, L06 7, L07 3.
